$\operatorname{Density}(\rho)=\frac{Z \times M}{N_A \times a^3}$<br/>Given,
$\begin{aligned}
& \rho=7.6 \mathrm{ g} / \mathrm{cm}^3 \\
& a=290 \times 10^{-12} \mathrm{ m} \\
& =290 \times 10^{-10} \mathrm{ cm}
\end{aligned}\begin{aligned}
& \therefore \quad \frac{7.6 \times 6.023 \times 10^{23} \times\left(290 \times 10^{-10}\right)^3}{56}=Z \\
